=94...[an observative] is usually stated by someone when they first
observe or take note of the relation, and wish to quickly communicate
it to someone else.=93

> =ABnu mi klama=BB is that, "look, [the event of] me coming" (=B1tense/asp=
ect/whatever).

"The event of me going" is not an observative, and I'm not sure what
you're saying with '(=B1tense/aspect/whatever).' Could you spell it out
for me?

> "never mind" is almost as long as ".i ko tolju'i" (for example), so, why =
new cmavo?

I don't think you understand my question. Firstly I'm not comparing
English and Lojban brevity. My use of "never mind" is to describe an
utterance that I wish to express distinctly in Lojban. My
illustrations were an attempt to show that this concept, a scalar
indicator from "make note" to "never mind," has common applications
similar to other BAI attitudinals. My question is: is there really no
attitudinal or cmavo for this concept? My syllogism is: if there is
not, then I wish to propose it as an experimental cmavo.

